{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And it shall go out.</b> [Meaning] the sale. Now, [the word] 'name' is in place of the adjective of the noun, and many like it. And after he mentioned 'dwelling-house,' we know that 'and sold from his possession' [refers to] a field or vineyard."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The lemma ויצא (\"and it shall go out\") quotes Leviticus 25:28's opening clause; Ibn Ezra glosses the implied subject as the sale. 'Name' (שם) here refers to the word שם ('there') in the verse, which he reads as functioning adjectivally; this is a technical grammatical point about its syntactic role."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:24.814283974Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}